  "institution": "MTSU",
  "courseName": "General Physics I (Mechanics)",
  "estimatedLength": "30 minutes",
  "objectives": [
    "Represent two-dimensional vectors using magnitude and direction, and translate between graphical vectors and x-y components.",
    "Add vectors graphically using the tip-to-tail method and identify the resultant vector.",
    "Decompose a vector into horizontal and vertical components using right-triangle relationships and reconstruct the original vector from its components.",
    "Explain why horizontal and vertical motions in projectile motion are independent when gravity acts only vertically.",
    "Describe how a projectile\u2019s horizontal velocity, vertical velocity, and position change during flight, including the instant of maximum height.",
    "Predict how launch angle and speed affect projectile trajectory, range, and maximum height, including the angle for maximum range at fixed speed."
